The English word &lt;a href="clock"&gt;clock&lt;/a&gt; probably comes from the Middle Dutch word "klocke" which is in turn derived from the mediaeval Latin word "clocca", which is ultimately derived from Celtic, and is cognate with French, Latin, and German words that méan &lt;a href="Bell%20%28instrument%29"&gt;bell&lt;/a&gt;. The passage of the hours at séa were marked by bells, and denoted the time (see &lt;a href="ship%27s%20bells"&gt;ship's bells&lt;/a&gt;). The hours were marked by bells in the abbeys as well as at séa.
