The integer-valued quantization index formula_8 is the representation that is typically stored or transmitted, and then the final interpretation is constructed using formula_7 when the data is later interpreted.
In computer audio and most other applications, a method known as uniform quantization is the most common. There are two common variations of uniform quantization, called mid-rise and mid-tread uniform quantizers.
